<title>GREECE: Alpha, Sigma lead Greek brokers in H1 market share.</title>
<headline>Alpha, Sigma lead Greek brokers in H1 market share.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens stock exchange member firm Alpha Brokerage led Greek brokers in cumulative first half market share with 8.27 percent of the bourse's trading volume, followed by Sigma Securities with 8.12 percent.</p>
<p>Based on statistics provided by the Athens stock exchange association of member brokers (SMEHA), trading volume in the first six months of 1997 totalled 4.636 trillion drachmas. versus 1.72 trillion in the first half a year earlier.</p>
<p>May turned out the first half's best month as volume reached 1.165 billion drachmas, or a quarter of total business for the period.</p>
<p>The quietest month was January with turnover of 528.7 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>SMEHA's statistics for the first six months of 1997 showed that large brokers continued to gnaw away market share from smaller firms.</p>
<p>The top five brokers shared 34.73 percent of the business, while the top 10 accounted for nearly half of total trading volume -- 49.07 percent.</p>
<p>There are 64 members in the Athens stock exchange.</p>
